  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The molarity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> orthophosphoric acid <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> having <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></math> purity by weight (specific gravity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.54</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>) is ______ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>. (Molar mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>98</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "11",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Specific gravity (density) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.54</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>cc</mi></math>.</p><p>Volume <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo> </mo><mi>ml</mi></math></p><p>Mass of solution <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.54</mo><mo>×</mo><mn>1000</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1540</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>%</mo></math> purity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p><p>So weight of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.7</mo><mo>×</mo><mn>1540</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1078</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math></p><p>Mole of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>mass</mi><mrow><mi>molar</mi><mo> </mo><mi>mass</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1078</mn><mn>98</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn></math></p><p>Molarity= <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>No</mi><mo>.</mo><mo> </mo><mi>of</mi><mo> </mo><mi>moles</mi><mo> </mo><mi>of</mi><mo> </mo><mi>solute</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Volume</mi><mo> </mo><mi>of</mi><mo> </mo><mi>solution</mi><mo> </mo><mi>in</mi><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Molarity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math></p>"
